hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1497","Abbad bin Yaqoub, whose opinion is trustworthy in his hadith, was accused. Amr bin Thabit and Al-Walid bin Abi Thawr told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Every person is required to pray every day,” so a man from the people said: This is one of the most severe things that you have brought to us. He said: “Enjoining what is right, and forbidding what is evil is a prayer, and your protection of the weak is a prayer, and your filthy retreat On the way is a prayer, and every step you take towards prayer is a prayer.”"
